  "kinetics": "change(t) / 1 mm = ell (1 - r(t)), r = exp(-(t - t1)/tau), t1 = 1 day, t in months, change = AL(t) - AL0 (positive is elongation): the law is unchanged at the reference time (zero start, generic eye model version 5); ell = context level + b (AL0 - 24.5 mm) / 1 mm",
  "hierarchy": "species -> treatment family -> treatment (contexts human/<treatment>/<family>; families control: single_vision, other; optical: orthokeratology, defocus_spectacles, multifocal_contacts; atropine: atropine, combination; light: red_light, outdoor; grouping (treatment, context)); an untrained treatment uses its family mean with the between-treatment variance added; each family arm of a study has its own study effect",
  "noise": "likelihoods and posteriors use the median of the studies' residual SDs as the noise centre; forecasts add independent noise so that their noise centre is the pooled residual variance (forecast_noise_pooling = pooled); forecasts carry each series' current deviation forward: 0.8 of the residual variance follows an Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process with a 12-month correlation time (deviation_fraction 0.8, deviation_months 12) in the per-series posteriors and predictive distributions, while the population (series summaries and REML) is fitted under working independence (deviation_in_population_fit false); initial states, which have no observation, are those of model 1.0.0",
  "scale": "the series hand the generic eye model the exact pseudo-fraction exp(change / 1 mm) and the pseudo-reference exp(AL0 / 1 mm); eye_additive_evaluation 5.0.0 rewrites every forecast, observation and interval in hundredths of a millimetre and recomputes the scores (1 pp = 0.01 mm)",
  "computation": "generic eye recovery model version 5 (model 2's exact mixture posteriors, REML population fit and predictive distribution with the one-column zero-start design) with harness version 7 (harness 6 with version-5 model calls): an 80-point tau grid 0.01..120 months, noise levels, Student-t nodes and robust components; point forecast = predictive median",
